.TH "INSPEKT\-PLUGINS" "7" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-plugins \- overview of the Inspekt plugin system
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspekt plugins are small JavaScript snippets \- typically imported from
bookmarklets \- that you can run inside the connected browser tab.
They are managed locally and never leave your machine.
.PP
Each plugin has a slug\-style ID (e.g.\ \f[B]text\-spacing\f[R]), an
optional category and tags, and metadata controlling how it is invoked:
whether it returns structured data, whether it auto\-runs on certain
domains, whether it is exposed as an MCP tool, and how long it may run
before timing out.
.PP
Plugins live in a SQLite database in the Inspekt data directory; see
\f[I]FILES\f[R] below.
.SH COMMANDS
The \f[B]inspekt plugin\f[R] command group manages plugins.
Common operations:
.TP
\f[B]inspekt plugin list\f[R]
Show every installed plugin, its category and tags.
.TP
\f[B]inspekt plugin add\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Add a new plugin from a bookmarklet URL or pasted JavaScript.
.TP
\f[B]inspekt plugin run\f[R] \f[I]ID\f[R]
Execute a plugin in the active tab.
.TP
\f[B]inspekt plugin export\f[R] / \f[B]import\f[R]
Move plugins between machines as JSON.
.PP
Run \f[B]inspekt plugin \(enhelp\f[R] for the full list, and \f[B]man
inspekt\-plugin\f[R] for detailed flags.
.SH AUTORUN
A plugin marked \f[B]autorun\f[R] executes automatically whenever the
page URL matches one of its \f[B]autorun_domains\f[R] patterns.
Inspekt debounces repeated triggers within a 3\-second window so that a
single page load only fires the plugin once.
.SH MCP EXPOSURE
A plugin with \f[B]mcp_exposed = true\f[R] is registered as an MCP tool
when the Inspekt MCP server starts, allowing AI agents to call it like
any other inspekt command.
Plugins that return structured JSON should also set \f[B]returns_data =
true\f[R] so that the MCP wrapper exposes the result.
.SH INSTALLED PLUGINS
This system man page does not list your installed plugins.
Run \f[B]inspekt plugin list\f[R] to see them, or \f[B]inspekt man
rebuild\f[R] to regenerate this page with an embedded \(lqINSTALLED
PLUGINS\(rq section under \f[I]\(ti/.local/share/man/man7/\f[R].
